# Raw input: He understood that unanimity and the requirement for supermajorities made collective action impossible. Now he also recognized that the majority might govern in its immediate interest rather than the "true" interest of the people. Whether these concerns might be reconciled— and if so, how—was the question on which the future of the United States rested.
